## Phase 2: Monophonic Note Manager (`note_manager.rs`)

### Problem
Wind instruments are inherently monophonic. When the player fingers a new note before releasing the previous one, the synth must handle this as a legato transition — not re-trigger envelopes. Standard polyphonic voice allocation is wrong for this use case.

### Implementation

```rust
pub enum NoteMode {
    /// Standard poly mode (bypass NoteManager, use existing voice allocator)
    Poly,
    /// Monophonic: always re-trigger envelopes, last-note priority
    Mono,
    /// Legato: only re-trigger on first note; pitch glides on held transitions
    Legato,
}

pub enum NoteEvent {
    /// New note, envelopes should re-trigger
    NewNote { note: u8, velocity: u8 },
    /// Legato transition, only pitch changes (envelopes continue)
    LegatoSlide { from_note: u8, to_note: u8, velocity: u8 },
    /// All notes released — begin release phase
    AllNotesOff,
}

pub struct NoteManager {
    mode: NoteMode,
    /// Stack of currently held notes (most recent = top). Max 10 entries.
    note_stack: [u8; 10],
    stack_size: usize,
    current_note: Option<u8>,
    portamento_active: bool,
}
```

**Requirements:**

1. `NoteManager` uses a **fixed-size stack** (no Vec, no heap). Maximum 10 simultaneous held notes is more than any wind controller can produce.

2. Note priority is **Last Note Priority** — always play the most recently pressed note. When that note is released, fall back to the previous note in the stack (if still held).

3. Implement `process_note_on(&mut self, note: u8, velocity: u8) -> NoteEvent`:
   - In `Poly` mode: always return `NewNote`
   - In `Mono` mode: always return `NewNote`, push to stack
   - In `Legato` mode: if stack is empty, return `NewNote`. If stack has notes, return `LegatoSlide { from: current, to: new }`

4. Implement `process_note_off(&mut self, note: u8) -> Option<NoteEvent>`:
   - Remove the note from the stack regardless of position
   - If the released note was the current playing note AND stack still has notes: return `LegatoSlide` to the new top-of-stack
   - If stack is now empty: return `AllNotesOff`
   - If released note was NOT the current playing note: return `None` (no audible change)

5. **Fingered Portamento** — separate struct:

```rust
pub struct PortamentoProcessor {
    current_pitch: f32,     // in semitones (MIDI note number, fractional)
    target_pitch: f32,
    rate: f32,              // semitones per sample
    active: bool,
    mode: PortamentoMode,
}

pub enum PortamentoMode {
    /// Always glide between notes
    Always,
    /// Only glide on legato transitions (fingered portamento)
    Fingered,
    /// Never glide
    Off,
}
```

6. Portamento time parameter: range 0ms–2000ms, labeled **"Glide Time"**. Convert to rate: `rate = semitone_distance / (time_ms * 0.001 * sample_rate)`. Rate must be recalculated on each new note based on the interval distance.

7. In `Fingered` mode: glide only occurs when `NoteEvent::LegatoSlide` is produced. On `NewNote`, pitch jumps immediately.

8. Write tests: legato detection, note stack overflow handling, portamento convergence.

