## AMENDMENT 5: Custom Curve Data Transfer (extends Phase 3 + Phase 7)

The standard `set_param(id, value)` mechanism sends a single f32. A custom breath curve requires transferring 128 f32 values (the lookup table).

For the Rust side:
```rust
impl BreathRouter {
    /// Receive a full custom curve table. Called from the UI bridge,
    /// NOT from the per-sample audio path.
    pub fn set_custom_curve(&mut self, table: &[f32; 128]) {
        self.custom_curve_table = *table;
    }
}
```

For the WASM bridge (Phase 7 integration):
- Use `wasm_bindgen` to expose `set_custom_curve` taking a `&[f32]`
- From the AudioWorklet, send the curve data via `MessagePort.postMessage` with a `Float32Array` (transferred, not copied)
- This is a one-time transfer when the user changes the curve, NOT per-sample

Do NOT try to encode 128 values as sequential single-param updates. That is fragile and slow.

