## AMENDMENT 9: NoteEvent Timing Precision (extends Phase 6)

The original spec defines `note_event: Option<NoteEvent>` in WindOutput. This is ambiguous about timing within a block.

Replace with:

```rust
/// Note events are timestamped relative to the start of the current block.
/// sample_offset = 0 means the event occurs at the first sample of the block.
pub struct TimestampedNoteEvent {
    pub event: NoteEvent,
    /// Sample offset within the current processing block (0..block_size-1)
    pub sample_offset: u32,
}
```

And in WindOutput:
```rust
pub note_events: [Option<TimestampedNoteEvent>; 4],  // max 4 events per block
pub note_event_count: usize,
```

This ensures legato transitions and note-off events are sample-accurate, not quantized to block boundaries. Without this, fast legato passages (common on EWI) will feel sluggish.

Check how the existing engine handles note events — if it already has a timestamped event queue, use that format instead of inventing a new one.

