## AMENDMENT 10: no_std Policy Clarification (extends Constraints section)

Revised policy:

The `wind/` module code that runs in the per-sample audio path MUST be allocation-free (no Vec, Box, String, HashMap in hot paths). This is non-negotiable for real-time audio safety.

However, the formal `#![no_std]` attribute is only required if the existing `engine/` crate already uses `#![no_std]`. If the engine crate uses `std` (check `engine/Cargo.toml` and `engine/src/lib.rs`), then forcing `no_std` on the wind module alone creates unnecessary build friction.

**Rule of thumb**: match whatever the engine already does. If engine is `no_std` with `libm`, wind is `no_std` with `libm`. If engine uses `std`, wind uses `std` but remains allocation-free in audio paths.

Before starting Phase 1, check:
```bash
grep -n "no_std\|extern crate\|use std" engine/src/lib.rs
cat engine/Cargo.toml | grep -A5 "\[dependencies\]"
```
And follow whatever convention is already established.